VERSION:

1.0	This project was a long time in the making. Many adjustments were
        made. There continues to be major bugs found in the code. Quite
        reasonable though if you look at the complexity of the program. I
        knew it would not be easy, only possible. The intro ANSI was done
        by Matt Benedict. Many thanks for his help with this as I'm no ANSI
        artist myself. I still have ideas for additional ANSI screens so if
        there are any ANSI artists out there...

2.0     (01-07-97) Would you believe I found a bug which kept the computer
        opponent from Going For The Knockout? Major bug! It was fixed.

	Improved and corrected many routines in version 2. Improved the
        computer manager. You'll see this as you fight against the
	computer. This was an important factor in one keeping the title
	from lesser opponents.

	Alot of the ANSI screens were dressed up to look better. Some
	routines were made to happen faster. Added the Title Belt ANSI for
	the champion to view.

	Added money routines so the boxers have something to fight for. If
	a fighter cannot beat the champ he can still make alot of money by
	holding second place. Also added increased money amounts for
	fighters with undefeated records. You also get more for fighting
	someone with an undefeated record.

	Added the champion ladder. You can no longer fight the top great
	heavyweight on your first bout. You must climb the ladder.

	Increased user file sizes to hold more records. Upgrading to 2.0
	means starting all over because the older files are no longer
	compatible.

	(02-02-97) So many changes today! The Hall of Fame is now complete.
        Of course you will not see anything until you have a great fighter.

	Dressed up all the log screens. Alternating between green and
        yellow allows you to read across these lines easily.

	Thomas Sherman passed suggested making all the text visible in the
        fast game. This is not feasible as it would no longer be a fast
        game. Instead I have added a computer pick to the regular game. If
        your not sure what to choose then the computer will do it for you.
        The computer picks are generated according to the averages. You
        will notice that sometimes your boxer comes out more aggressive.
        This is because the computer compares the numbers for
        both fighters and realizes your fighters only chance is to score
        big early. In the normal fight screen where it shows the corner
        mans guess, you will see a number by the prompt. This is the
        fighter control factor. If it is lower than your opponents then he
        will throw more punches and hence, outscore you in the long run.
        These numbers do change and the computer realizes the changes.

	Corrected an error in the sysop menu. When you retired a user it
        eliminated his boxer but not the records. Then when the user
        created a new fighter it would have the old records still.

	Added the Owners listing with a sort routine. When a user retires a
        boxer his money is added to his account. If he is not on the user
        list then he will be added when he retires his first boxer. From
        then on his score is updated.

	Changed the quote list. Now all comments are colored green. When
        there are champion fights, the results are added automatically and 
        in yellow. Unsuccessful bids for the title are not added. All
        fights against the pros are added.

	I know I've forgot to list many changes here but there are so many.
        I've made a complete overhaul and I may well be doing it again
        after hearing more comments on this version. Please send in your
        comments.

2.5     (22 April 97) Fixed a bug where a fighter could have his control
        factor reduced by more than 2.

	Added a feature where each fight is now sanctioned. No fights will
	be allowed (sanctioned) if the challenger has three more defeats
	than he has wins against any one fighter. I put this in due to the
	fighters always fighting the champion even if they knew they would
        lose time after time.

	Added a feature where fighters cannot challenge boxers after they
        suffer 10 losses. This will be evaluated to see it's impact on the
	game. The intent is to limit their time in the game to successful
        fighting.

	Added a feature where you can select the person you want to fight
	by merely typing his ranking number. This turned out to be easier
	than expected, probably due to the additional files added to the game 
	over time. I had thought of this from the first however I gave up
	on the idea because of the way I was accessing files. Thomas
	Sherman's suggestion that this be added put it on my plate once
	again. Thanks for the help Tom. I have left the view any fighter
	screen to type in names as it allows viewing the All-Time greats
	records also.

	Added the fighters records to the rankings list. This was another
	idea from Thomas Sherman. The screen certainly had room for
	improvement and the records add to it nicely.

        Changed the GETNUM routine to a cnet standard numeric input. These
	prompts will not allow letters to be input and may serve to catch
	the users of previous version when trying to type in a name. I find
	myself doing it a lot.

2.5a    Held tournament for all the great boxers and saved their records.

        Added option of viewing a fighters fightlist or not. Some list can
        be pretty long and tedious to view everytime.

	Added the auto computer fight. This way you can see every punch
        without having to select strategies. The strategies are still
        computer selected.

3.0     (22 June 1997) All fighters can now fight against the "Great
        Fighters". The payment for these fights are not as high as the
        current champion would be paid for them.

        (4 July 1997) Change to the last entry. The program now checks if
        you will be denied to fight the two fighters ranked directly
        over yours. If you are not allowed to fight them because of three
        or more losses to them then you are taken directly to fight one of
        the greats. If this status changes and someone goes ahead of you
        that you can fight then you will have to fight them. The goal is
        that you will always be able to fight someone till you have 10 losses.
        After 10 losses you will have to retire. With this option, if you
        are unseated as the champion and you are unsuccessful to regain the
        title in three tries, then you are allowed to proceed to fight the
        greats to achieve the all-time greats list. You must have beaten a
        level 11 fighter to gain this status.

	(26 July 1997) Added a sort routine to the Great fighter's listing.
        It was just listing them in order of their entry into the list. It
        should now sort them according to the money won in their career.

	Additional bug fixing in the routines for checking if you could
        fight the boxers above you. Sometimes it would let you fight the
        greats when there was a normal fighter you could fight.

	(16 October 1997) Fixed bugs with the fighters records not
        recording all the fights he was involved in. This was caused by
        another bug that ended the program prematurely.

	(16 October 1997) Fixed the bug That was not scoring the owners
        listing correctly. This was due to the way the game identifies the
        users according to their account number and not their handles. This
        needed to be addressed in the game for users who were not currently
        logged on, thus the creation of the "base" directory. This records
        each users account number and handle upon logging on. If the
        account number is already present then it checks to make sure the
        person has the same handle and if not it gets updated. This was
        added for people who change their handle or account numbers being
        reassigned to other users. This data will not be changed in the
        owners listing as it will list two different users from the same
        account due to a handle or account change. There is no good way to
        facilitate this so sysops will have to find a way to keep updated
        with a text editor.

	(22 October 1997) Dressed up the owners listing to be more
        readable. It has it's limits as to money amount and length of the
        user's handle. If you run out of room and know arexx then some
        adjustments to line 1618 will correct it.

	(24 October 1997) Added a hints page for users to get some helpful
        hints about their newly created boxer. This is also available after
        viewing a fighter's record. Also added an additional line to the boxer
        files for tracking purposes. Will have to make an update file to ease
        updating previous versions.

	Finished the updating file. The update file changes each fighter
        file to have 48 lines. If your having problems, check that each
        fighters file is 48 lines. This file also adds the "Base"
        directory. The Base directory is used to keep track of users names
        with their handles. Every time a user enters the game this file is
        checked if it exists and if not it is automatically added. If it
        does exist then the name within is check with the current user to
        make sure they are the same. If they are not then the file is
        updated. This was neccessary for the owners listing. The checking
        of the name prevents a mix up when a user is deleted from the BBS
        and a new user gets that account number. The update file executes
        automatically when the game is started or Maint runs. It copies a
        file from the SysOp directory to the the Box directory called
        updated. The updated file is protected and must remain in the Box
        directory. If it is not there then it will try to update again and
        possibly screw up the number of lines in the boxer files.

	(25 October 1997) Added the styles for each fighter in the rankings
        list. This helps you decide who you would like to fight against.
        This feature is automatically added to previous versions of the
        game as it is played.


**IMPORTANT NOTICE**

	The workbench sort command: This command sorts text files from 0-9
        or a-z. This was not good as the high score list usually want the
        high numbers on top. I found a sort replacement on aminet called
        lsort.lha which I've included in this archive. Copy the command
        lsort to your c: directory. This command allows the same commands
        as the original command with a few more options, namely "reverse"
        sorting which this game uses. The game will look for lsort in your
        c: path.

**IMPORTANT NOTICE**

	Changed the Slam Wall to the News Wall. This seemed appropriate
        since title fights are added automatically. It is still available
        for users to add comments to. Changed what will be automatically
        added to the wall. Before it would add comments if someone took the
        title or if they fought one of the Greats. Now it will show the
        results of all title fights and results of the Champion fighting
        the Greats. Results posted here are color coded to match the event.
        Users comments are still green. Changed the automatic comments to be
        more colorful.

	Improved the View Champions List to give more complete details.

	(8 November 1997) Added Records listing for the following
        categories;

	Best Undefeated Record
	Most Career Knockdowns
	Most Career Knockouts
	Most Rounds Fought
	Most 1 Round Knockouts
	Most Title Defenses
	Most Career Bouts

	Only fighters with less than 15 losses are eligible for these
        records. (You can only fight with less than 10 losses.) Records 
        are updated when a user enters the game and when he finishes a bout.
        Therefore, non-active users are not eligible either. The records list
        can be viewed by pressing 8 at the main menu.

FUTURE IMPROVEMENTS:

  Still taking any suggestions from users and SysOps for improvement. Any
suggestions that seem workable will be considered.

  Considering adding great fighter biographies so users will know a little
about the fighter, especially the ones they never heard of.
 Considering a system where a fighter can block one fighter from
challenging him. The block would be able to be overcome after some time.
 Considering an option to give advice to users on how to fight other
fighters depending on both fighters abilities.
